Portions of SWIFT v8 derived from Decepticon (with the changes described
below) include:

  * swift/agent/langgraph_layer/                 -- multi-agent layer scaffold
    and the sixteen specialist prompt definitions inspired by
    decepticon/agents/standard/*.
  * swift/sandbox/tmux_session.py                -- libtmux-based interactive
    session wrapper modeled on decepticon/sandbox_kernel/tmux.py.
  * swift/engagement/{soundwave,opplan,conops}.py
                                                 -- engagement-planning
    workflow modeled on Decepticon's RoE/ConOps/OPPLAN generation.
  * swift/deploy/compose.yaml                    -- multi-service lab stack
    inspired by Decepticon's docker-compose.yml.

Changes from upstream:
  - Re-implemented on a slimmer abstraction (no LangGraph dependency in the
    default install; a MiniGraph runner walks the same DAG topology). When
    `langgraph` is installed it can take over.
  - LiteLLM routing is optional (env-driven), not required.
  - Neo4j attack graph is optional; default backend is SQLite + NetworkX.
  - All external tool invocations are gated by SWIFT's existing ROE
    (swift/security/roe.py) rather than Decepticon's middleware stack.


2. claude-bug-bounty  --  https://github.com/shuvonsec/claude-bug-bounty
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) shuvonsec
Licensed under the MIT License.

Portions of SWIFT v8 derived from claude-bug-bounty include:

  * swift/skills/agents/swift-*.md               -- vendored skill files (8),
    prefixed `swift-` to avoid namespace collisions.
  * swift/skills/commands/swift-*.md             -- vendored slash commands
    (23), prefixed `swift-`.
  * swift/bounty/hunt_memory.py                  -- cross-engagement audit /
    pattern / journal stores, modeled on the upstream `memory/` package.
  * swift/bounty/auth_session.py                 -- session-token propagation
    into httpx/katana/ffuf/nuclei, modeled on the upstream
    `tools/auth_session.py`.
  * swift/bounty/validator.py                    -- 7-question + 4-gate
    finding validator, codified from the upstream `agents/validator.md`.
  * swift/bounty/report_formats.py               -- H1 / Bugcrowd / Intigriti
    / Immunefi report formatters, derived from the upstream
    `agents/report-writer.md` templates.
  * swift/bounty/web3/                           -- smart-contract auditor
    (slither/mythril/patterns), inspired by the upstream `web3/` skill set.

Changes from upstream:
  - Rewritten in Python (the upstream is a mix of Bash + Python skill files).
  - Integrated with SWIFT's ROE gate and audit log.


